  "description": "LIGHTNESS ABOVE ALL\n\nHigh-Modulus Carbon Fibres (Toray T1100 and T800) In the evo carbon lay-up, more high-module fibers have been used to achieve a record weight.\n\nOUTSTANDING AGILITY\n\nIts ultracompact chainstays, only 420 mm, ensure agility and stunning acceleration. The perfect combination of stability on descents and reactivity on climbs. It also features a dropout with a similar appearance to the BH road bikes, more solid and compact, which reduces the width of the rear chainstays by 2 cm.And it gives the frame's new lines a stylish and sleek appearance.\n\nMAXIMUM STIFFNESS\n\nSo that you can generate maximum power with each turn of the pedal.\n\nBUILT-IN SADDLE CLAMP\n\nFor a 31.6 mm seat post, compatible with standard-sized telescopic seat posts.\n\nICR INTERNAL CABLES\n\nThe cables are inside the ICR steering to achieve 100% internal cabling. The result: an Ultimate Evo with a cleaner, sharper and more functional style that allows the rider to focus on the trail.\n\nFLAT MOUNT TECHNOLOGY\n\nThe BH Ultimate features countless little details. It comes with a bracket for the Flat Mount brake clamp, to help ensure a light weight and the best possible integration . Despite its minimalist design, the frame has been designed to comfortably withstand the stress produced by the rear brake.",
